Z||000011||BAM-BAM||05-01-2000||09:45 PM||||   Thanks peoples, that's the info I needed. Now, is that only late modles or... how far back can I go? This is all helpfull when the time comes. Let me get this right; I'll need the complete motor, the wiring harness and the ECM, correct? Let me know!!!! TIA <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000012||RobertVol||05-01-2000||10:17 PM||||You will need the complete engine...<P>Wiring harness will have to be adapted/ ACE or Chris West can probably get you in the right direction on that. ALso You may want to put in some cost for tranny mods. I changed and upgraded my clutch(Centerforce) I figured when you spend this much dont quibble over a couple of extra hundred dollars <P>I believe the engines go back to 1992. I believe the 92 Bonneville had the SC engine.<BR> <BR>But I disagree with alot of people who think go to a junk yard or find a donor. I found mine from a dealer who had spare from a bad order at a local buick dealer. The engine was intact basically brand new. I spent 1400.00 for everything. Why spend 500 - 700 for the engine and take the risk? <P>Anyway my two cents ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Phil||05-01-2000||10:19 PM||||Check <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A>   he has a good run down on the different 3800s||||reg||1
Z||000014||Dan86gt3.8||05-02-2000||05:02 AM||||Hey rob are you new here?  what are you packin?  I have a 3.8 serries II, with a 4t60e tranny, and I did it with an ace kit.  How about you?<P>Anywho you will need all this stuff:<BR>-Motor with accesories(ie altenator,ac pump)<BR>-the 4t60e tranny if you are going automatic<BR>-complete uncut engine wiring harness and the harness to the 4t60e if you are going that direction<BR>-the ecm<BR>-the diagnostic link (error code checker plugin deal)<BR>-the first 3 feet of the exhaust pipe that bolts to the manifold <BR>-the cv joints (once again if going with 4t60e)<BR>thats all I can think of for now.  And about the years they were produced you can find info on ace's sit I think, but basically the earlier the year model the lower hp/torque it had.  The best ones are 95+ models where the eitgh digit (I think its the 8th)in the vin number of the car is a "k".  thees were rated at 265hp.  Anyways if you got any other questions send them my way <BR>||||reg||1
